<?xml version="1.0"?>
<?xml-stylesheet type="text/xsl" href="http://jsbsim.sf.net/JSBSimScript.xsl"?>
<runscript
       name="Mi-17 cold and dark, then startup"
       xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
       xsi:noNamespaceSchemaLocation="http://jsbsim.sf.net/JSBSimScript.xsd">

  <description>
    Two phases in one run: 15 minutes (900s) fully cold and dark
    (battery, generators, and hydraulic pumps all off, engines never
    started, controls neutral -- identical state to scripts/test_mi17_
    cold_and_dark.xml), then a startup transition at t=900s that turns
    electrical/hydraulic power back on and starts both engines,
    followed by 30 minutes (1800s) to see the aircraft sit at steady
    ground-running RPM for an extended period after the initial spin-up
    settles, not just through the settle transient itself; run ends at
    t=2700s (900 + 1800).

    A real, notable result from the shorter (180s post-start) version
    of this script: engine start after 900s cold-and-dark does NOT
    ramp up smoothly from 0 the way scripts/test_mi17_ground_run_idle.
    xml's immediate-start-at-t=0 case does. It spikes to ~329.5 RPM
    (above the 192 target) at the instant propulsion/set-running fires,
    then decays back down through ~303 (t+2s) -> ~199 (t+10s) -> ~187
    (t+30s) -> ~192 (t+60-90s), settling cleanly with no further
    oscillation. A brief nose-gear contact was also logged ~0.135s
    after the startup event (h-agl-ft dipping to ~3.3 ft before
    recovering to the same ~4.74 ft steady baseline test_mi17_ground_
    run_idle.xml settles to) -- a small, self-correcting bounce from
    the start transient, not a crash. The 30-minute extension here is
    partly to confirm that settled state is genuinely durable over a
    much longer post-start window, not just stable for the ~90-120s
    scripts/test_mi17_ground_run_idle.xml originally measured.

    Same governor-driven approach as that script: fcs/throttle-cmd-norm[0/1]
    is never set directly here either, only propulsion/set-running;
    the governor (rpm_governor.xml, always loaded on this aircraft)
    drives throttle on its own. Collective stays flat and bias stays
    zero for the whole run -- this demonstrates the cold-dark-to-
    running electrical/engine transition, not a climb-out, so there is
    no collective-bias ramp or climb-collective ramp here the way
    scripts/test_mi17_hover.xml has.

    electrical/main-generator-on, hydraulic/main-pump-on, and hydraulic/
    emergency-pump-on are restored to 1.0 at the startup transition
    (electrical/backup-generator-on and hydraulic/backup-pump-on stay
    at 0.0) to match this aircraft's own file defaults in electrical_
    system.xml/hydraulic_system.xml -- i.e. "normal running
    configuration", not an arbitrarily chosen subset.

    Known model limitation, carried over from test_mi17_cold_and_dark.
    xml: electrical/battery-voltage-v and hydraulic/main-pressure-bar
    are not actually wired to these -on switches (electrical/main-
    voltage-v and hydraulic/main-pressure-bar are bare constant
    properties in their respective Systems files, never recomputed
    from switch state), so those two traces will stay flat across the
    t=900s transition in the output CSV even though the switches
    themselves visibly step from 0 to 1 there. The switch properties
    are included in the CSV specifically so the transition timing is
    still visible even though its electrical/hydraulic *effect* isn't
    modeled.
  </description>

  <use aircraft="mi17" initialize="reset00"/>

  <!-- CSV trace of the full run, 5 Hz; see test_mi17_hover.xml's
       identical pattern for why this is a script-scoped output rather
       than something added to aircraft/mi17/mi17.xml. 5 Hz over 2700s
       is ~13500 samples; still a modest file (a few hundred KB to
       ~1 MB of CSV text), and gives plenty of resolution for both the
       15-minute cold-and-dark hold and the startup/spin-up transient
       without needing a higher rate. -->
  <output name="mi17_cold_dark_to_startup.csv" type="CSV" rate="5">
    <property> position/h-agl-ft </property>
    <property> attitude/pitch-rad </property>
    <property> attitude/roll-rad </property>
    <property> velocities/p-rad_sec </property>
    <property> velocities/q-rad_sec </property>
    <property> velocities/r-rad_sec </property>
    <property> gear/unit[0]/WOW </property>
    <property> gear/unit[0]/compression-ft </property>
    <property> gear/unit[0]/compression-velocity-fps </property>
    <property> gear/unit[1]/WOW </property>
    <property> gear/unit[2]/WOW </property>
    <property> propulsion/gearbox[0]/shaft-rpm </property>
    <property> propulsion/engine[0]/n1 </property>
    <property> fcs/throttle-cmd-norm[0] </property>
    <property> propulsion/engine[0]/output-torque-lbft </property>
    <property> propulsion/engine[0]/thrust-lbs </property>
    <property> electrical/battery-on </property>
    <property> electrical/battery-voltage-v </property>
    <property> hydraulic/main-pump-on </property>
    <property> hydraulic/main-pressure-bar </property>
  </output>

  <run start="0.0" end="2700.0" dt="0.0075">

    <event name="hold cold-and-dark" persistent="true">
      <!-- Same state as test_mi17_cold_and_dark.xml, held only while
           sim-time-sec is under 900.0; see the "startup" event below
           for the t=900 transition. Engines are never started here
           (no propulsion/set-running command in this event). -->
      <condition> simulation/sim-time-sec le 899.999 </condition>
      <set name="fcs/collective-cmd-norm" value="0.0"/>
      <set name="fcs/adj/collective-bias" value="0.0"/>
      <set name="fcs/rudder-cmd-norm" value="0.0"/>
      <set name="fcs/aileron-cmd-norm" value="0.0"/>
      <set name="fcs/elevator-cmd-norm" value="0.0"/>
      <set name="fcs/throttle-cmd-norm[0]" value="0.0"/>
      <set name="fcs/throttle-cmd-norm[1]" value="0.0"/>
      <set name="ap/attitude-hold-on" value="0.0"/>
      <set name="ap/altitude-hold-on" value="0.0"/>
      <set name="electrical/battery-on" value="0.0"/>
      <set name="electrical/main-generator-on" value="0.0"/>
      <set name="electrical/backup-generator-on" value="0.0"/>
      <set name="hydraulic/main-pump-on" value="0.0"/>
      <set name="hydraulic/backup-pump-on" value="0.0"/>
      <set name="hydraulic/emergency-pump-on" value="0.0"/>
    </event>

    <event name="checkpoint cold-dark 1s" persistent="false">
      <condition> simulation/sim-time-sec ge 1.0 </condition>
      <notify>
        <property> simulation/sim-time-sec </property>
        <property> position/h-agl-ft </property>
        <property> gear/unit[0]/WOW </property>
        <property> gear/unit[0]/compression-ft </property>
        <property> electrical/battery-on </property>
        <property> electrical/battery-voltage-v </property>
      </notify>
    </event>

    <event name="checkpoint cold-dark 300s" persistent="false">
      <condition> simulation/sim-time-sec ge 300.0 </condition>
      <notify>
        <property> simulation/sim-time-sec </property>
        <property> position/h-agl-ft </property>
        <property> propulsion/gearbox[0]/shaft-rpm </property>
        <property> electrical/battery-on </property>
      </notify>
    </event>

    <event name="checkpoint cold-dark 600s" persistent="false">
      <condition> simulation/sim-time-sec ge 600.0 </condition>
      <notify>
        <property> simulation/sim-time-sec </property>
        <property> position/h-agl-ft </property>
        <property> propulsion/gearbox[0]/shaft-rpm </property>
        <property> electrical/battery-on </property>
      </notify>
    </event>

    <event name="checkpoint cold-dark 899s (end of 15min hold)" persistent="false">
      <condition> simulation/sim-time-sec ge 899.0 </condition>
      <notify>
        <property> simulation/sim-time-sec </property>
        <property> position/h-agl-ft </property>
        <property> attitude/pitch-rad </property>
        <property> attitude/roll-rad </property>
        <property> propulsion/gearbox[0]/shaft-rpm </property>
        <property> electrical/battery-on </property>
        <property> electrical/battery-voltage-v </property>
        <property> hydraulic/main-pump-on </property>
        <property> hydraulic/main-pressure-bar </property>
      </notify>
    </event>

    <event name="startup: power on, start engines" persistent="false">
      <!-- Fires once at t=900.0, the moment hold-cold-and-dark above
           stops re-asserting the off state every frame (its own
           condition, sim-time-sec le 899.999, goes false the frame
           before this one fires, so there is no one-frame fight
           between the two events over the same properties).

           Starts the main engines via FGTurboshaft's starter-cmd/
           cutoff-cmd, not propulsion/set-running: the latter forces full
           throttle directly and converges to a steady state inside a
           single frame via FGPropulsion::GetSteadyState(), producing the
           ~329 RPM one-frame overshoot documented in this script's own
           description above. starter-cmd/cutoff-cmd drive the real
           per-frame phase machine instead, so the governor actually gets
           to moderate throttle throughout. Unlike test_mi17_ground_run_
           idle.xml, no extra delay is needed here before engaging them:
           this event already fires at t=900.0, long past the one-frame
           tsTrim-transition window near t=0 that requires that delay
           (see that script's own comment for why). Engine 2 (tail rotor)
           stays on its own simple per-engine set-running, same reasoning
           as that script: FGElectric has no phase state machine to get
           stuck in. -->
      <condition> simulation/sim-time-sec ge 900.0 </condition>
      <set name="electrical/battery-on" value="1.0"/>
      <set name="electrical/main-generator-on" value="1.0"/>
      <set name="hydraulic/main-pump-on" value="1.0"/>
      <set name="hydraulic/emergency-pump-on" value="1.0"/>
      <set name="propulsion/engine[0]/starter-cmd" value="1"/>
      <set name="propulsion/engine[1]/starter-cmd" value="1"/>
      <set name="propulsion/engine[0]/cutoff-cmd" value="0"/>
      <set name="propulsion/engine[1]/cutoff-cmd" value="0"/>
      <set name="propulsion/engine[2]/set-running" value="1"/>
      <notify>
        <property> simulation/sim-time-sec </property>
        <property> electrical/battery-on </property>
        <property> hydraulic/main-pump-on </property>
        <property> propulsion/gearbox[0]/shaft-rpm </property>
      </notify>
    </event>

    <event name="hold collective flat through spin-up" persistent="true">
      <!-- Same governor-driven approach as test_mi17_ground_run_idle.
           xml: collective flat, no forced throttle, only propulsion/
           set-running (already commanded once above) and letting
           rpm_governor.xml drive fcs/throttle-cmd-norm[0/1] on its
           own from here. -->
      <condition> simulation/sim-time-sec ge 900.0 </condition>
      <set name="fcs/collective-cmd-norm" value="0.0"/>
      <set name="fcs/adj/collective-bias" value="0.0"/>
    </event>

    <event name="checkpoint startup +2s" persistent="false">
      <condition> simulation/sim-time-sec ge 902.0 </condition>
      <notify>
        <property> simulation/sim-time-sec </property>
        <property> propulsion/gearbox[0]/shaft-rpm </property>
        <property> propulsion/engine[0]/n1 </property>
        <property> fcs/throttle-cmd-norm[0] </property>
        <property> position/h-agl-ft </property>
      </notify>
    </event>

    <event name="checkpoint startup +10s" persistent="false">
      <condition> simulation/sim-time-sec ge 910.0 </condition>
      <notify>
        <property> simulation/sim-time-sec </property>
        <property> propulsion/gearbox[0]/shaft-rpm </property>
        <property> propulsion/engine[0]/n1 </property>
        <property> fcs/throttle-cmd-norm[0] </property>
        <property> velocities/r-rad_sec </property>
      </notify>
    </event>

    <event name="checkpoint startup +30s" persistent="false">
      <condition> simulation/sim-time-sec ge 930.0 </condition>
      <notify>
        <property> simulation/sim-time-sec </property>
        <property> propulsion/gearbox[0]/shaft-rpm </property>
        <property> propulsion/engine[0]/n1 </property>
        <property> fcs/throttle-cmd-norm[0] </property>
        <property> velocities/r-rad_sec </property>
      </notify>
    </event>

    <event name="checkpoint startup +60s" persistent="false">
      <condition> simulation/sim-time-sec ge 960.0 </condition>
      <notify>
        <property> simulation/sim-time-sec </property>
        <property> propulsion/gearbox[0]/shaft-rpm </property>
        <property> propulsion/engine[0]/n1 </property>
        <property> fcs/throttle-cmd-norm[0] </property>
        <property> velocities/r-rad_sec </property>
      </notify>
    </event>

    <event name="checkpoint startup +90s" persistent="false">
      <condition> simulation/sim-time-sec ge 990.0 </condition>
      <notify>
        <property> simulation/sim-time-sec </property>
        <property> propulsion/gearbox[0]/shaft-rpm </property>
        <property> propulsion/engine[0]/n1 </property>
        <property> fcs/throttle-cmd-norm[0] </property>
        <property> velocities/r-rad_sec </property>
      </notify>
    </event>

    <event name="checkpoint startup +180s" persistent="false">
      <condition> simulation/sim-time-sec ge 1080.0 </condition>
      <notify>
        <property> simulation/sim-time-sec </property>
        <property> propulsion/gearbox[0]/shaft-rpm </property>
        <property> propulsion/engine[0]/n1 </property>
        <property> propulsion/engine[0]/output-torque-lbft </property>
        <property> position/h-agl-ft </property>
      </notify>
    </event>

    <!-- Extended-hold checkpoints, added when this script's post-start
         window was extended from 180s to 30 minutes (1800s): confirm
         the governed RPM stays durably at 192 over a much longer
         window than the initial spin-up settle, watching for the same
         kind of slow ITT/torque thermal creep documented (and treated
         as expected, not divergence) in scripts/test_mi17_spinup_diag.
         xml's own long full-throttle hold. -->
    <event name="checkpoint startup +5min" persistent="false">
      <condition> simulation/sim-time-sec ge 1200.0 </condition>
      <notify>
        <property> simulation/sim-time-sec </property>
        <property> propulsion/gearbox[0]/shaft-rpm </property>
        <property> propulsion/engine[0]/n1 </property>
        <property> propulsion/engine[0]/output-torque-lbft </property>
        <property> position/h-agl-ft </property>
        <property> attitude/pitch-rad </property>
        <property> attitude/roll-rad </property>
      </notify>
    </event>

    <event name="checkpoint startup +10min" persistent="false">
      <condition> simulation/sim-time-sec ge 1500.0 </condition>
      <notify>
        <property> simulation/sim-time-sec </property>
        <property> propulsion/gearbox[0]/shaft-rpm </property>
        <property> propulsion/engine[0]/n1 </property>
        <property> propulsion/engine[0]/output-torque-lbft </property>
        <property> position/h-agl-ft </property>
      </notify>
    </event>

    <event name="checkpoint startup +15min" persistent="false">
      <condition> simulation/sim-time-sec ge 1800.0 </condition>
      <notify>
        <property> simulation/sim-time-sec </property>
        <property> propulsion/gearbox[0]/shaft-rpm </property>
        <property> propulsion/engine[0]/n1 </property>
        <property> propulsion/engine[0]/output-torque-lbft </property>
        <property> position/h-agl-ft </property>
      </notify>
    </event>

    <event name="checkpoint startup +20min" persistent="false">
      <condition> simulation/sim-time-sec ge 2100.0 </condition>
      <notify>
        <property> simulation/sim-time-sec </property>
        <property> propulsion/gearbox[0]/shaft-rpm </property>
        <property> propulsion/engine[0]/n1 </property>
        <property> propulsion/engine[0]/output-torque-lbft </property>
        <property> position/h-agl-ft </property>
        <property> attitude/pitch-rad </property>
        <property> attitude/roll-rad </property>
      </notify>
    </event>

    <event name="checkpoint startup +25min" persistent="false">
      <condition> simulation/sim-time-sec ge 2400.0 </condition>
      <notify>
        <property> simulation/sim-time-sec </property>
        <property> propulsion/gearbox[0]/shaft-rpm </property>
        <property> propulsion/engine[0]/n1 </property>
        <property> propulsion/engine[0]/output-torque-lbft </property>
        <property> position/h-agl-ft </property>
      </notify>
    </event>

    <event name="final checkpoint startup +30min (t=2700s)" persistent="false">
      <condition> simulation/sim-time-sec ge 2699.9 </condition>
      <notify>
        <property> simulation/sim-time-sec </property>
        <property> propulsion/gearbox[0]/shaft-rpm </property>
        <property> propulsion/engine[0]/n1 </property>
        <property> fcs/throttle-cmd-norm[0] </property>
        <property> propulsion/engine[0]/output-torque-lbft </property>
        <property> propulsion/engine[0]/thrust-lbs </property>
        <property> position/h-agl-ft </property>
        <property> attitude/pitch-rad </property>
        <property> attitude/roll-rad </property>
        <property> velocities/r-rad_sec </property>
        <property> gear/unit[0]/WOW </property>
        <property> gear/unit[1]/WOW </property>
      </notify>
    </event>

  </run>

</runscript>
